--
-- Every numeric item traces to the seismolord teaching oracle and reproduces
-- the live NG7 Expert capstone answer key: the wedge tuning of an equal and
-- opposite SAND pair (+0.08 / -0.08) from 0 to 60 ms at 2 ms, read at 25 Hz
-- and 40 Hz. Tuning thickness 16 ms and 10 ms (both graded exactly), tuning
-- amplitude 0.1155947595834732 at BOTH frequencies (the same Float64 value,
-- because 25 x 16 = 40 x 10 = 400 Hz ms and the Ricker depends on frequency
-- and thickness only through their product), isolated reflector amplitude
-- 0.07999999821186066 (= Math.fround(0.08)), theoretical tuning thickness
-- sqrt(6)/(2 pi f) = 15.593936024673521 ms. Same pipeline
-- src/lib/seismolordTeaching.js drives and wedgeLab.test.js pins, on the
-- shared @petrolord/engines rockphysics wedge engine.
--
-- Tier note: the Associate tier (DC7) BUILT the synthetic and owns the
-- 15/25/40 Hz amplitude and time table; the Professional tier (DC18) owns the
-- bulk shift scan and the 66 ms peak-time swing. This tier does not re-teach
-- either. It owns the wedge as a controlled experiment, the tuning curve, the
-- f*T law, the resolution limit, the apparent-thickness floor, theory versus
-- a gridded model, and the Gassmann-to-AVO chain that module 6 hands to the
-- Rock Physics ladder. Module 4 supplies the MECHANISM behind the "2 ms
-- sampling artefact" DC7 named without explaining.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences and within-pool near-duplicates before seeding,
-- per DC12 and DC13.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert,
-- so learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path; the ON
-- CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on re-seeds.
-- Re-seeding replaces the whole bank for this course-tier; fine while there
-- are no open attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
--
-- Ladder note: an ADVANCED enrollment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a seismolord
-- professional cert in-transaction.
--
-- NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('seismolord', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-wedge-experiment","title":"The Wedge Experiment","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-why-a-wedge-and-not-a-well","l03-the-equal-and-opposite-pair","l04-the-model-as-built","l05-the-wedge-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-two-reflections-meeting","title":"Two Reflections Meeting","lesson_keys":["l01-the-thick-end","l02-the-composite-trace","l03-thinning-past-isolation","l04-when-the-pair-shares-a-sign"]},{"key":"m03-the-tuning-curve","title":"The Tuning Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-reading-the-curve","l02-the-tuning-thickness","l03-the-amplitude-at-tuning","l04-one-amplitude-two-thicknesses","l05-where-the-peak-actually-sits"]},{"key":"m04-frequency-and-resolution","title":"Frequency and the Resolution Limit","lesson_keys":["l01-the-forty-hertz-curve","l02-one-curve-in-disguise","l03-why-the-two-amplitudes-match","l04-bandwidth-buys-thickness","l05-apparent-thickness-has-a-floor"]},{"key":"m05-theory-and-the-grid","title":"Theory and the Grid","lesson_keys":["l01-kallweit-and-wood","l02-the-grid-cannot-land-on-it","l03-the-rules-of-thumb-compared","l04-what-a-check-against-theory-buys"]},{"key":"m06-using-the-wedge","title":"Using the Wedge","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-the-same-sand-with-a-different-fluid","l05-from-one-angle-to-many","l06-the-top-of-the-ladder"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
